From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:06:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the pinned message's avatar is centred on its card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The card that pins the turn's user message at the top of the
conversation (0102, minimized and expandable since 0109) drew its
avatar at the top of its row: the header was items_start, and the row
is taller than the icon -- the expand toggle, an IconButton, sets its
height whenever the message has a second line or does not fit, and the
text sits in its own padded inner area (§6.46). The operator saw the
icon ride high on the minimized card (2026-11-20).

Minimized, the row now centres its children, so the avatar, the line
and the toggle share one axis. Expanded, they keep to the top, where
the message starts reading; a centred icon beside a scrolled block of
text would point at nothing.

The avatar is wrapped in a div carrying the debug selector
thread-pinned-user-message-avatar, which is what the tests measure.

Tests (thread_view::tests::pinned_avatar_tests, new): the avatar's
centre is within 1px of the card's on a one-line message, and on a
two-line message, where the toggle is shown.

Amended for Zeo proposal §6.66 (ask 89, 2026-11-22): the avatar still
moved. Minimized the row centred it beside the 22 px toggle, expanded it
kept to the top, so the 14 px icon jumped up about 4 px on every expand
(measured: 41 px -> 37 px in the test below). The row now keeps to the
top in both states, and the avatar sits in a box as tall as the toggle,
so it is centred on the minimized line and stays beside the first line
when the card opens. The body gets the same minimum height, centred only
while minimized, so the line does not shift by its own pixels either.
The height is one constant, PINNED_ROW_HEIGHT, which is also the
toggle's button size, so the three cannot drift apart.

Test (thread_view::tests::pinned_avatar_tests, added):
the_avatar_stays_put_when_the_card_expands -- the avatar's top moves by
at most 0.5 px across an expand. Red seen: "the avatar moved 4px".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
